HackForge 2.2.0: design skills (impeccable + ui-ux-pro-max)

Drafted in Harness (ClaudeCodeUI). Paths are relative to the HackForge plugin root (the folder with
.claude-plugin/plugin.json), made against HackForge 2.1.1 as bundled in resources/hackforge.

Apply in your HackForge repo:
    git apply --3way /path/to/ClaudeCodeUI/docs/hackforge-design-skills.patch
Then refresh Harness's bundled copy:
    npm run hackforge:sync

What it changes:
- build writes one DESIGN.md design system before frontend work (style picked with ui-ux-pro-max
  when it's available) and freezes it with the contracts.
- The builder agent gets the Skill tool; frontend builders load impeccable and run design-scan
  before returning.
- New `hf-run.sh tools design-scan [paths]`: impeccable's anti-pattern detector, recorded as
  .hackforge/evidence/design-scan.json. Harness passes the launcher in HARNESS_IMPECCABLE; it also
  finds a Claude Code plugin install, ~/.impeccable or PATH. Not installed -> not_observed.
- Verifier captures it, verify maps quality findings to major and repeated slop to minor, the
  experience judge and the UI rubric use it, VERIFY.md gets a short section, perfect's UX lens uses it.
- Version 2.2.0, CHANGELOG and README.

